## Never-do reminders / quirks (host-measured)

- `tools/science_funnel/terrain.py` sha256 is PINNED by the terrain receipt
  manifest — never edit it casually; put companions beside it.
- Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads BOM-less UTF-8 .ps1 as ANSI: an em-dash in a
  string becomes a smart quote and breaks parsing. Keep .ps1 ASCII-only.
- `git show <rev>:<path> | Set-Content` MANGLES newlines; extract files with
  bash redirection (`git show rev:path > path`) instead.
- PowerShell `[double]` parameter binding rounds to 15 digits — comparing
  engine readouts must be done on RAW JSON text, not parsed doubles.
- `& python ... 2>&1` under `$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'` promotes native
  stderr to terminating errors — drop to 'Continue' around expected refusals.
- `Get-Content`/`Add-Content` without `-Encoding` on PS 5.1 treat BOM-less
  UTF-8 as ANSI — handoff sections appended through them get mojibake;
  do file surgery through the venv Python with explicit encodings.
- Background exec tasks on this host can be reaped with the stdout log left
  empty and NO completion notification; a full-suite run that outlives ~5
  minutes is safer CHUNKED into foreground module runs, or re-checked via its
  log after the fact (both full-suite runs eventually completed exit 0).
- Graph JSONs re-shard when the store rebuilds — after authored edits run
  `build_graph.py` then `--check-only`, commit the whole data/ set atomically,
  and on rebase take master's store side + replay the idempotent build.
- Another lane's engine may be alive on this host (a foreign chimera_engine
  PID was observed). Kill ONLY your own PID after the path guard.

