## Gotchas for the next agent (this checkout)

- The host is SHARED and heavily loaded (12+ foreign python processes observed);
  single modules can take 13+ minutes (test_macaque_anatomy 793 s). Background
  exec tasks get REAPED (empty log, exit -1, no notification) — run long modules
  in FOREGROUND calls with a generous timeout, one module per call, and never pipe
  native output through Select-Object (it buffers until exit; use a redirect to a
  log file and read the file).
- `unittest discover -p <module>` per module is the safe chunk shape; the full
  suite in one process exceeds any single exec window under this load.
- project_spec.py MUST be invoked as a module (`-m tools.creature_graph.project_spec`),
  not as a script path.
- The scene bundle embeds the store graph hash under /graph_hash AND /graph_file
  (the graph_<hash>.json copy name) — EVERY store rebuild moves the scene digest.
  If your lane rebuilds the store, re-pin DEFAULT_SCENE_PORTABLE_SHA256 deliberately
  with the diff proof (graph-hash-only) IN THE SAME COMMIT.
- Extract a historical store via `git ls-tree -r --name-only <rev>` + `git show
  <rev>:<path>` through a python subprocess (binary-safe) into an aside dir, then
  CreatureGraph.load from there. Label aside copies: a copy made from a working
  tree holds whatever the tree held at copy time (this bit me once — a "baseline"
  aside that was actually my own store).
- The pinned interpreter has numpy/pandas but NO openpyxl and must not gain
  packages (never pip-install into E:\PythonChimera); parse xlsx with the stdlib
  zipfile+ElementTree readers that visual_proof_wave2.py and adapters_muscle.py
  already carry.

